  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "comment": "Autoclave at 121ºC. Cool to 55ºC and aseptically add the following:"
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "comment": "**Horse serum should be heat inactivated at 56ºC for 30 minutes."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 7,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 8,
      "comment": "When making with agar, be sure to warm serum and yeast extract solution to 55ºC before adding to basal medium."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 9,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 10,
      "comment": "Final pH should be 7.4. Dispense as desired."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 11,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 13,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 14,
      "comment": "Mix together for 10 minutes, autoclave at 121ºC. Let stand overnight."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 15,
      "comment": "Transfer yeast solution to centrifuge bottles and spin at 9,000 rpms for 50 minutes."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 16,
      "comment": "Carefully pour supernatant into 100 ml bottles and discard the cell debris."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 17,
      "comment": "Autoclave at 121ºC and store sterile at 2-8ºC."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 18,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 19,
      "comment": "*Note: As of 10/26/2011 Gibco Yeast Extract is no longer in use. Gibco changed the supplier of their raw materials as of early 2011. This new version no longer supports growth and has been replaced with Yeast Extract #3."
    }
  ]
}